      "writtenOn": "2020-09-29T19:16:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wasn\u0027t sure if this isn\u0027t a documentation issue or not. When presenting Rd, the other side can be either open or be presenting Open, Rp_usb, Rp_1.5, or Rp_3.0. so VSTATE_CCx must allow for this differentiation:\n\nVSTATE_CCx |  CCx\n-----------|---------------------\n     0     |   0 -\u003e CC_VOLT_OPEN\n     1     |   5 -\u003e CC_VOLT_RP_DEF\n     2     |   6 -\u003e CC_VOLT_RP_1_5\n     3     |   7 -\u003e CC_VOLT_RP_3_0\n\nSo this is why I check for STM32_UCPD_SR_VSTATE_RA so that 0 maps to 0, then add 4 for the other 3 results.\n\nThe other thing to note is that UCPD can\u0027t present Ra on the line so if ANMAMODE \u003d 1, then ucpd is presenting Rd.",
      "parentUuid": "0f0b2ff7_b23eb7c8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 165,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 165,
        "endChar": 13
      },
