      "writtenOn": "2020-09-29T19:16:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately, it\u0027s been long enough that I can\u0027t remember this 100% clearly now, but I have been looking at table 415 in RM0440 again today, and I think what I have is correct. I found that table to be very confusing, but I felt by the end, I understood how to decode this.\n\nVSTATE_CCx can only return 0, 1, 2, or 3\nwhen presenting Rp (anamode \u003d\u003d 0 or the else case), VSTATE_CCX \u003d\u003d 3 means N/A and this maps most closely to TYPEC_CC_VOLT_OPEN and so if vstate_ccx \u003d\u003d 3, then ccx \u003d 0. This is what that \"if\" check is for.\n\nif VSTATE_CCX !\u003d 3, then the following mapping applies:\n\nVSTATE_CCx | CCx               |  Equation\n-----------------------------------------------------------\n     0     |  1 \u003d CC_VOLT_RA   |  (0 + 1) % 3 \u003d 1\n     1     |  2 \u003d CC_VOLT_RD   |  (1 + 1) % 3 \u003d 2\n     2     |  0 \u003d CC_VOLT_OPEN |  (2 + 1) % 3 \u003d 0",
      "parentUuid": "02d00615_c57b7397",
